<body>
    <h1>Sub-advisor analysis notes</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"Subadvisoranalysisnotes-PlatformAccess"><span style=3D"font-s=
ize: 20.0px;letter-spacing: -0.008em;">Platform Access</span></h1>
    <p><strong>Scenario 1: PM sub-advisors who are our client</strong></p>
    <ul>
     <li>Users will be set under their =E2=80=98primary firm=E2=80=99 and l=
inked to the firms of their sub-advising accounts as their =E2=80=98seconda=
ry firm(s)=E2=80=99</li>
     <li>Users only have limited Account feature access on their sub-advisi=
ng accounts</li>
     <li>Users must have trading capability and be able to do individual tr=
ade orders, trade allocation and basket booking on their primary accounts a=
nd sub-advising accounts on the same view - &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link=
" href=3D"mailto:joseph.kim@nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">@Kim, Joseph</a><span>=
&nbsp;</span>This is referred as the =E2=80=98aggregated=E2=80=99 view of O=
rder module. Owen and I can update you about this</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><strong>Scenario 2: PM sub-advisors who are not our client</strong><=
/p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"691acab1-b5db-4e6d-a96b-0d7929e99a6a">e.g. SGGG</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"e56f37c4-d336-4fa9-9f8d-bdb7ba545d2d">Users will be s=
et under the firm of their sub-advising accounts for white-labelling and fi=
rm-specific settings</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"45e76166-5934-44f6-98ff-de28bf6269db">However, they m=
ust only have limited Account feature access on their sub-advising accounts=
 but full trading capability.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"17416961-bee9-41bc-a0f5-96210719e117"><a class=3D"ext=
ernal-link" href=3D"mailto:varun.anand@nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">@Anand, Var=
un</a><span>&nbsp;</span>Question - Though this user has one firm only, I t=
hink the =E2=80=98assignment type=E2=80=99 should be marked as =E2=80=98S=
=E2=80=99 to indicate that their assigned RR code ranges are =E2=80=98PM su=
b-advisory RR codes=E2=80=99 (as opposed to primary rr codes). What do you =
think? Thanks.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Anti use-case</strong></p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"7567ebe1-da55-40ed-ad26-c1283bc0d796">System access -=
 NDEX Systems</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4b38b35c-ea3c-4af8-b1f3-21b806bdf2e0">Ex-Employee acc=
ess with no clean-up (e.g. Inthirai&nbsp;@ WA)</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Sampling</strong></p>
    <ol>
     <li data-uuid=3D"358bd4cd-aa80-47ee-b8d5-457507d667fe">Non-firm&nbsp;<=
/li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"583bc4cb-ceec-44b7-a6d5-2cd65896ce7b">Standard, singl=
e different parent</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4b0e25ac-ec07-4ef9-a808-296a3b5f31e6">Standard, multi=
ple parents (3 or more)</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ca538790-fbd9-4e58-bd29-cf0a2768f6c6">Edge cases =E2=
=86=92 over-provisioned access beyond trading</li>
    </ol>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><strong>Problems To Solve</strong></p>
    <ol>
     <li data-uuid=3D"d9d900af-f583-4614-9371-7ceb80edf174">Person identifi=
cation - no unique ID, relies of fuzzy matching may result in data breaches=
</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"c7c033a2-edc3-49a5-afc2-bd83e5b34acb">Unclear relatio=
nships between firms with no ability to supervise</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"04871026-f1c9-4733-afaf-a5cfdf74eeb4">Provisioning pr=
ocess / standards historically have been inconsistent, leading to profile d=
iscrepancies&nbsp;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"79a62126-3221-4383-a24f-27194dcefe03">:question: Numb=
er of consistencies across systems where e.g. SZ provisions MORE access tha=
n NetRep and R2</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"7e4aafd7-62c7-4fc0-9c9e-a40b89b228f0">Historical inco=
nsistent user setup practices lead to mismatches in first/last names</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"916eb074-ba2f-4c54-b7df-944008132fbd">Backdoor access=
 for system providers&nbsp;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"b7dda4cc-9de4-49c3-bba9-30fee651a449">Firm-level acce=
ss for sub-advisors is currently not supported (looks like there may be use=
 cases for this)</li>
    </ol>
    <p><br></p>
    <h2 id=3D"Subadvisoranalysisnotes-PlatformInteractions">Platform Intera=
ctions</h2>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"6815e4ea-ee1e-4622-9b90-7a588e193b24">:question:&nbsp=
; How does a PM actually work with their sub-advisor??&nbsp; Need to do som=
e interviews.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"5a6f2c9c-dc20-40a4-bcf3-b343c4c874fc">:question:&nbsp=
; Do they all have the same accesses?&nbsp; &nbsp;Data analysis of R2 + SZ =
+ NR required.=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"3a165976-f062-42ac-ba02-e66934806207"><span style=
=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Are there different usage profiles for differen=
t sub-advisory relationships?</span></li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"dff333ba-ec7a-4e1f-8a04-b2c6431d06ef">Would the fir=
ms want us to help restrict a "standard sub-advisor" profile, how do they g=
overn sub-advisor accesses and activities</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"Subadvisoranalysisnotes-OperationalScenarios">&nbsp;Operation=
al Scenarios</h1>
    <p><br></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 879.24px;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 184.077px;">
       <col style=3D"width: 190.704px;">
       <col style=3D"width: 271.698px;">
       <col style=3D"width: 231.981px;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"col" style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" c=
lass=3D"confluenceTh">
         <ol>
          <li data-uuid=3D"ec623c8c-d946-40db-8fcb-8b2dc2847383">Already ou=
r client</li>
         </ol></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" c=
lass=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p><span>2. Not our client</span></p></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" c=
lass=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p><span>3. Edge case</span></p></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" c=
lass=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p><span>4. Emergent termination</span></p></th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <ul>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"6ab3b012-d7a1-4627-ab6=
f-d70762c5d839">
           <p><span>They already have a CX id</span></p></li>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"9e6b3d88-978b-470b-9eb=
e-4d6cd42caa28">
           <p><span>Required to update the profile to allow PM sub-advising=
 activities</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p><span>Required to create a CX id for them</span></p>
         <ul>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"1cb0105d-b4c0-4186-aa2=
c-9d8a1b6f1c88">
           <p><span>Under which firm id?</span></p></li>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"32daae36-e0dd-4f1e-ba8=
9-6ca9d8b3fc9c">
           <p><span>How to prevent the sub-advisor to have full access to c=
lient accounts</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p><span>They was not our client but sub-advising for other PM fir=
ms, then become our client (i.e. 2. becomes 1.)</span></p>
         <ul>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"264025b3-36f5-42b0-9bb=
6-379d39ad5022">
           <p><span>Required to transfer their CX id to their firm and set =
up their home firm user access in addition to the PM sub-advising access</s=
pan></p></li>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"098b99a4-53df-4a3b-bfe=
1-8c0ea7ae2abb">
           <p><span>The case should be surfaced through the client implemen=
tation process and be flagged</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <ul>
          <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"21fd8021-979e-4a24-bdd=
f-dfb6559b93db">
           <p><span>There is a situation that the PM sub-advisors must not =
be able to access their client accounts entrusted to them</span></p>
           <ul>
            <li class=3D"paragraph-child">
             <p><span>How to update firm &amp; user settings intra-day?</sp=
an></p></li>
           </ul></li>
         </ul>
         <p><br></p></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"Subadvisoranalysisnotes-UseCases">Use Cases</h1>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 97.2355%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 14.7231%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 46.8206%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Use Cases of PM Sub-advisor</th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Onboarding</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Cannot access any onboarding capabilities of accounts under sub=
-advising RR codes</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Trading&nbsp;</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Can trade on accounts pertained to my su=
b-advising RR codes</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
        <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">PM Sub-advisors have full =
trading rights just like the home firm advisors</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Account Admin Services</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Cannot submit client/account update requests</p>
          <p>Cannot submit servicing requests (e.g. withdrawl instructions,=
 etc)</p>
          <p>Can submit systematic plan instruction requests&nbsp;</p>
          <p>Can submit Trade Cancel/Correction instruction requests <span =
style=3D"color:#f87168;">- See Stanley's reply below&nbsp;</span></p>
          <p>Can initiate or stop DRIP&nbsp;</p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Client &amp; Account Inquiry</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Can view the <strong>basic client info (NOT the Confidential d=
ata, e.g. SIN #, home address, bank account #) - same as Trader role</stron=
g></p>
          <p>Can view the<strong> account portfolio info </strong>about the=
 accounts under sub-advising RR codes <strong>- same as Trader role</strong=
></p>
          <p><strong>Requirement: A PM sub-advisor is supposed to view clie=
nt/account info which are relevant to trading activities <time datetime=3D"=
2023-02-06" class=3D"date-past">06 Feb 2023</time>&nbsp;</strong></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p class=3D"auto-cursor-target">.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><br></p>
    <p><strong>From:</strong> Kwong, Stanley &lt;stanley.kwong@<a class=3D"=
external-link" href=3D"http://nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">nbc.ca</a>&gt; <br><=
strong>Sent:</strong> Wednesday, October 19, 2022 12:46 PM<br><strong>To:</=
strong> So, Candi &lt;Candi.So@<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://nb=
c.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">nbc.ca</a>&gt;; Norris, Raymond &lt;Ray.Norris@<a cl=
ass=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">nbc.ca</a>&gt=
;<br><strong>Cc:</strong> Lam, Penny &lt;penny.lam@<a class=3D"external-lin=
k" href=3D"http://nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">nbc.ca</a>&gt;; Ahmed, Bilal &lt=
;bilal.ahmed@<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofol=
low">nbc.ca</a>&gt;<br><strong>Subject:</strong> Sub-advisor relationship -=
 Background and Approach</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>Hi Candi,</p>
    <p>As discussed a month back, I am providing more guidance on what has =
been decided on specifically to how we treat sub-advisors.&nbsp; I will be =
updating <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://can01.safelinks.protect=
ion.outlook.com/?url=3Dhttps%3A%2F%2Fjira.bnc.ca%2Fbrowse%2FRDB-1095&amp;da=
ta=3D05%7C01%7CCandi.So%40nbc.ca%7C2ea9ce5f8f5c4b94315b08dab1f15944%7Cc2115=
7cabce341a88aa7a23c4639610a%7C0%7C0%7C638017947380925333%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbG=
Zsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C=
3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=3DtyGAvgHaHH0ubkjpDYSb36qHj9%2BFUjuHZIYDOPBe85E%3D&=
amp;reserved=3D0" rel=3D"nofollow">https://jira.bnc.ca/browse/RDB-1095</a>,=
 with the same content after this email.</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><u>Background:</u></p>
    <p>A sub-advisor / advisor relationship is where the advisor owns the c=
lient relationship and performs non-portfolio management activities where-a=
s the sub-advisor has the portfolio management responsibility (trading / tr=
ade allocation) for the client but do not own the underlying relationship.&=
nbsp; Sub-advisor does not bear the administration responsibilities to the =
account.&nbsp; I.E.&nbsp; they do not take instructions or perform request =
administration such as cash withdrawal or contribution from the client or t=
he advisor.</p>
    <p><strong>At NBIN, we may have sub-advisors who are also advisors for =
their own client accounts.</strong></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><u>Capabilities of the sub-advisor:</u></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>A sub-advisor <u>currently have and will continue to have</u> the fo=
llowing capabilities with respect to their activities at NBIN for RR Codes =
they are sub-advising:</p>
    <ul>
     <li>Order entry and submission for all asset classes</li>
     <li>Order list / status view</li>
     <li>Submission of a Mutual Funds Basket</li>
     <li>Submission of a Trade Advice for trade allocation</li>
     <li>View Client ID level information (Read only)</li>
     <ul>
      <li>Client Profile</li>
     </ul>
     <li>View Account level information (Read only)</li>
     <ul>
      <li>Account Profile</li>
      <li>transaction history</li>
      <li>holdings</li>
     </ul>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>A sub-advisor <u>WILL NOT have</u> the following capabilities for th=
e RR Codes they are sub-advising:</p>
    <ul>
     <li>Access to statements, confirmations or tax documents of client</li=
>
     <li>Client Onboarding</li>
     <li>Direct access to iMost / SOMA.&nbsp; This means for the sub-adviso=
r they cannot submit:</li>
     <ul>
      <li>MF Trade Correction</li>
      <li>DRIP instruction submission</li>
     </ul>
